---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/BeforeAfter.astro';
import Gauge from '../../components/Gauge.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/ContactBand.astro';
import { STORY, SITE, AUTHOR, BUSINESS } from '../../data/site';
const url = `${SITE}/work/the-story-group/`;
const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${url}#article`,
    headline: 'A recruiting firm’s website, rebuilt to be found',
    description: 'How The STORY Group went from an aging Wix site, slow on mobile and hard to find for anything but its own name, to a fast custom build with a page for each specialization.',
    datePublished: '2026-07-01',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@id': AUTHOR.id },
    publisher: { '@id': BUSINESS.id },
    mainEntityOfPage: url,
    about: { '@id': 'https://storygroup.ca/#org' },
    image: [`${SITE}/work/storygroup-after.webp`, `${SITE}/work/storygroup-before.webp`],
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    '@id': 'https://storygroup.ca/#org',
    name: STORY.client,
    url: STORY.clientUrl,
    description: 'A recruiting firm in Oakville, Ontario, specializing in finance, supply chain, and procurement.',
    address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Oakville', addressRegion: 'ON', addressCountry: 'CA' },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Review',
    '@id': `${url}#review`,
    itemReviewed: { '@id': BUSINESS.id },
    reviewBody: STORY.quote,
    datePublished: STORY.quoteDate,
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: STORY.person, jobTitle: STORY.role, worksFor: { '@id': 'https://storygroup.ca/#org' } },
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Case Study: The STORY Group Website Rebuild | Colin Robey"
  description="How an Oakville recruiting firm went from an aging Wix site, slow and hard to find, to a fast custom site with a page for each specialty, built to be found in Google and read by AI assistants."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Work', href: '/work/' }, { name: 'The STORY Group', href: '/work/the-story-group/' }]}
  schema={schema}
  image="/work/storygroup-after-1080.webp"
  imageAlt="The rebuilt storygroup.ca homepage"
  type="article"
  published="2026-07-01"
  modified="2026-07-25"
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-hero" style="padding-bottom:2rem">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/work/">Work</a><span>/</span><span>The STORY Group</span></nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Website rebuild &amp; SEO</p>
        <h1>A recruiting firm’s website, rebuilt to be found.</h1>
        <p class="lead">The STORY Group had an aging Wix site: slow on mobile, and turning up for little beyond its own name. Here’s the rebuild, and what the first three months looked like.</p>
        <div class="case-meta" style="margin-top:1.5rem"><span class="chip">Recruiting</span><span class="chip">Oakville, ON</span><span class="chip">Wix → custom build</span><span class="chip">Live at <a href="https://storygroup.ca/" rel="noopener" style="margin-left:.3em">storygroup.ca</a></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section--tight" style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="wrap"><BeforeAfter eager /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section--tight band-pine" aria-label="Results at a glance">
      <div class="wrap" style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:2rem 4rem; align-items:center">
        <div class="gauges" style="margin:0">
          <Gauge value={STORY.speedBefore} label="Mobile speed, before" variant="before" />
          <span class="gauge-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <Gauge value={STORY.speedAfter} label="Mobile speed, after" variant="after" />
        </div>
        <ul class="ticks" style="max-width:52ch; color:var(--on-pine)">
          <li><strong style="color:var(--on-pine)">98/100 on mobile, 100 on desktop</strong><span style="color:var(--on-pine-soft)">Anyone can check it by running storygroup.ca through PageSpeed.</span></li>
          <li><strong style="color:var(--on-pine)">Inquiries it can finally track</strong><span style="color:var(--on-pine-soft)">Separate forms for candidates and for companies hiring, captured and counted.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>The challenge</h2>
        <p>The STORY Group’s site was an aging Wix build. It had the usual pages (home, about, team, services, partners) but the homepage was thin, and there were no dedicated pages for the three areas the firm specializes in: finance, supply chain, and procurement. Those are the pages that would need to rank, and they didn’t exist.</p>
        <p>It was also slow on mobile, and page speed is one of the signals Google weighs, so a slower site gets held back against faster competitors. It carried no analytics at all, so there was no way to see what was working. Most of the search traffic it did get came from people already looking for The STORY Group. Someone searching “supply chain recruiter in Toronto” wasn’t landing on them.</p>
        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>I rebuilt the site on a fast, modern foundation the firm owns outright, with no monthly platform subscription and no template ceiling. Finance, supply chain and procurement each got a dedicated page, so each can be found and rank on its own. It’s built with the structured data and clean markup that help Google and AI assistants understand the firm, and it’s quick to load.</p>
        <p>It’s also measured properly for the first time, with analytics, Search Console, and separate contact forms for candidates and for companies hiring, so decisions run on real data rather than guesses. Ian brought the knowledge of his business and his market; I brought the build and the systems. We shaped it together.</p>
        <h2>What happened next</h2>
        <p>The first three months point in the right direction, with the caveat that this is a boutique firm with a Canadian audience, so the numbers are modest in absolute terms. The forms now capture real inquiries the old site couldn’t track at all: mostly candidate résumés, and the first inquiries from companies looking to hire.</p>
        <p>It has also started turning up for the supply-chain, procurement and logistics searches the old site used to miss, though it’s early days and most of that is still on page two. It ranks first for the firm’s own name, and the next step is moving those higher-intent pages onto page one.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section band-paper2" aria-label="Client testimonial">
      <div class="wrap">
        <blockquote class="quote quote--paper" style="max-width:62ch">
          <p>{STORY.quote}</p>
          <footer><span><strong>{STORY.person}</strong>{STORY.role}, {STORY.client}</span></footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactBand heading="Want a site built to be found like this?" body="A fast, modern site your business owns, built to be found in Google and in AI answers. Builds start at $6,500 and every one is scoped differently, so tell me what you’re trying to fix and we’ll start with a short call." service="Website design and build (from $6,500), from case study" messageLabel="What are you trying to fix?" />
  </main>
</Base>
